an effect row whole (heaven_and_earth_witness): {'en': "heaven and earth called to witness — the STATUS the case's evidence clause writes on Israel: 'I call heaven and earth to witness against you this day that you shall surely perish quickly from the land … you shall not prolong your days upon it but shall be utterly destroyed' (Deut 4:26) — the witnesses of the exile case (4:25-31: corrupt → perish, scatter, few, serve wood and stone; seek → find; return → mercy); the Sifrei 306:1's CHAIN OF WITNESSES — 4:26 the third of eleven (30:19 'I call heaven and earth to witness against you this day', 31:28 'that I may call heaven and earth to witness against them', 32:1 'give ear, O heavens'; 30:19's first seven words identical, computed); 'the end of days' (4:30) a prophecy — no timer, no exile written; Gittin 88a:15-17 and Sanhedrin 38a:6 (the exile hastened by two years of 'grown old'); Megillah 31b:2 (the Ninth of Av's reading)", 'he': 'הַעִידֹתִי בָכֶם הַיּוֹם אֶת הַשָּׁמַיִם וְאֶת הָאָרֶץ (I call heaven and earth to witness against you this day — Deut 4:26)', 'ledger_op': 'status', 'ink': "Deut 4:26 ('I call heaven and earth to witness against you this day'), 4:25 ('when you beget sons and sons' sons and have grown old in the land and deal corruptly'), 4:27-31 (the arms), 30:19, 31:28, 32:1 (the chain — forward); Leviticus 26:33, 26:42 (the tochacha's scatter and remember — the first tellings, by CALL), 28:36, 28:64 (forward); Onkelos 4:26; the Sifrei 306:1 on 32:1 (read at the reading); Babylonian Talmud Gittin 88a:15-17, Sanhedrin 38a:6, Megillah 31b:2", 'corpus': 'deu_04_obey_horeb (STEP_Dt_4_25 through STEP_Dt_4_31; the claim DV04A-04)', 'exam': 'cold_run_obey_horeb.py (F4 the_exile_case — the_case_head, the_witnesses, perish_and_scatter, seek_and_find, in_your_distress_return, the_merciful_god; the tape kind witnesses_called)'} | (entered_the_covenant): {'en': "entered the covenant — the STATUS the sprinkled blood writes on the people: 'behold the blood of the covenant which the LORD has cut with you upon all these words' — the entry the convert repeats (circumcision, immersion, the blood: Keritot 9a, Yevamot 46b; Mishnah Keritot 2:1's convert lacking atonement until the blood is sprinkled)", 'he': 'וַיֹּאמֶר הִנֵּה דַֽם הַבְּרִית אֲשֶׁר כָּרַת יְהוָה עִמָּכֶם (and he said: behold the blood of the covenant which the LORD has cut with you — Exod 24:8)', 'ledger_op': 'status', 'ink': "Exod 24:8 ('the blood of the covenant' — the phrase at Exod 24:8 and Zech 9:11 alone; 'and he threw it on the people'), 24:6 ('half the blood... in basins' — the basin-word at Exod 24:6 and Song 7:3 alone), 24:5 (the youths' burnt and peace offerings), 24:7 ('we will do and we will hear' a hapax); Zech 9:11 (the second seat: 'by the blood of your covenant'); Onkelos Exod 24:8 ('to ATONE for the people'; 'which the LORD CUT with you'); Babylonian Talmud Keritot 9a:9 (the entry rite), Yevamot 46b:4 (no sprinkling without immersion)", 'corpus': 'exo_24_covenant_ascent (STEP_Ex_24_5, 24_6, 24_8)', 'exam': "cold_run_erection.py; Mishnah Keritot 2:1 (the convert), Keritot 8b:18 (the convert's offering an olah like 24:5's)"} | (blessing_and_curse_set): {'en': "the blessing and the curse set — the STATUS the line blessing_and_curse_set writes on Israel: 'SEE, I SET BEFORE YOU TODAY A BLESSING AND A CURSE: the blessing, if you hearken to the commandments of the LORD your God which I command you this day; and the curse, if you do not hearken to the commandments of the LORD your God and turn aside from the way which I command you this day, to go after other gods whom you have not known' (11:26-28) — 7:12-16's conditional (hearing_blessed on the tape, blessings_for_hearing on Israel) made A PAIR named and set before the people (the singular imperative 'see' over 'before you' plural — the register's both; 30:15's 'see, I have set before you today life and good, death and evil' and 30:19's 'choose life' the pair's own run forward — the Sifrei 53:1's crossroads, 54:1); 'turn aside from the way' 9:12's calf (not_righteousness by CALL); 'other gods whom you have not known' 13:3's and 13:14's phrase; idolatry the denial of the whole Torah (the Sifrei 54:4; Sotah 37a the ceremony's curse on the graven image first); the choice each day against the inclination (Sukkah 52a:5, 52a:13); the scale of merit — one commandment tilts the world (Kiddushin 40b:1-2); 11:31-32's 'possess it and dwell in it' (Kiddushin 26a:10 — an act of acquisition; Ketubot 110b:7, 110b:23 — the dwelling weighed, the Sifrei 80:4-5) and 'keep to do all the statutes and the judgments which I set before you today' (4:8's pair, 12:1 reopens — obey_horeb by CALL)", 'he': 'רְאֵה אָנֹכִי נֹתֵן לִפְנֵיכֶם הַיּוֹם בְּרָכָה וּקְלָלָֽה (see, I set before you today a blessing and a curse — Deut 11:26)', 'ledger_op': 'status', 'ink': "Deut 11:26-28 (the pair set), 11:31-32 (the crossing, the possession, the dwelling, the charge); Deut 7:12-16 (hearing_blessed — seven_nations by CALL), 8:19-20 (good_land.the_testimony by CALL), 9:12 (turn aside from the way — not_righteousness by CALL), 4:8 (obey_horeb by CALL), 13:3, 13:14, 30:1, 30:15-20 (the pair's run forward), 27:12-13; Joshua 8:34; Onkelos 11:26-28; Babylonian Talmud Sotah 32a:5-6, 37a:11, 37b:1-6; Kiddushin 26a:10, 40b:1-2; Ketubot 110b:7-15, 110b:23-24, 111a:1-8; Sukkah 52a:5, 52a:13; the Sifrei on Deuteronomy 53-54, 80", 'corpus': 'deu_11_bless_curse_set (STEP_Dt_11_26 through STEP_Dt_11_28, STEP_Dt_11_31, STEP_Dt_11_32; the claims DV11-01 through DV11-06)', 'exam': "cold_run_blessing_and_curse.py (F5 the_blessing_and_the_curse — see_i_set_before_you, the_blessing_if, the_curse_if, possess_and_dwell, the_dwelling_weighed, keep_to_do; the exam kind blessing_curse_case; the status written on the tape kind blessing_and_curse_set at the counter's day)"} | (became_the_lords_people_this_day): {'en': "Israel became the LORD's people this day — the STATUS the line people_this_day_declared writes on Israel: 'be silent and hear, O Israel: THIS DAY YOU HAVE BECOME A PEOPLE TO THE LORD YOUR GOD' (27:9) — 26:17-19's mutual declaration MADE A STATUS on the day; Onkelos 'a people BEFORE the LORD'; 'be silent' once in the Bible, Onkelos 'attend and hear'; the Sifrei 291:6-7's 'Dt.27:9' the translator's misprint for 25:9 — no shelf row on the verse; the readback row VARIANT against the tape's covenant_offered (Exodus 19:5) and the covenant formula's own line", 'he': 'הַיּוֹם הַזֶּה נִהְיֵיתָֽ לְעָם לַיהוָה אֱלֹהֶֽיךָ (this day you have become a people to the LORD your God — Deut 27:9)', 'ledger_op': 'status', 'ink': "Deut 27:9, 26:17-19 (this runner's own line); Exodus 19:5-6 (exodus_story — the offer, the reference); Onkelos 27:9", 'corpus': 'deu_26_bikkurim_close (STEP_Dt_26_1 through STEP_Dt_26_19; claims DV26-01 through DV26-03), deu_27_ebal_curses (STEP_Dt_27_1 through STEP_Dt_27_26; claims DV27-01 through DV27-04), deu_28_blessings (STEP_Dt_28_1 through STEP_Dt_28_14; claims DV28A-01 through DV28A-04), deu_28_curses_a (STEP_Dt_28_15 through STEP_Dt_28_44; claims DV28B-01 through DV28B-05) and deu_28_curses_b (STEP_Dt_28_45 through STEP_Dt_28_69; claims DV28C-01 through DV28C-05)', 'exam': 'cold_run_firstfruits_ebal_curses.py (F5 the_people_this_day — this_day_you_have_become_a_people_to_the_lord; the line people_this_day_declared) — THE LEAN PASS: the exam the twenty-six Mishnah rows the ledger cites (deu_26_28_ki_tavo_exam_2026-09-26.md)'} | (confessed): {'en': "confessed — the status entry that opens the recovery branch: the iniquity and the fathers' iniquity confessed; the Sifra's 'as soon as they confess I return and have mercy'", 'he': 'וְהִתְוַדּוּ אֶת־עֲוֺנָם וְאֶת־עֲוֺן אֲבֹתָם (and they shall confess their iniquity and the iniquity of their fathers — Lev 26:40)', 'ledger_op': 'status', 'ink': 'Lev 26:40 (probe והתודו fired); the humbled heart at 26:41 (יכנע)', 'corpus': 'lev_26_bless_curse (LV26-26 confession and the humbled heart)', 'exam': 'cold_run_tochacha.py (the recovery gate); Sifra Bechukotai Chapter 8 3, 8 5'}
